    "knowledge_point": "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form",
    "problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form.",
